WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.529
Why is the government trying to ban

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.539
TikTok, the popular social media

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.309
app which is owned by ByteDance, a

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.229
Chinese company, has come under fire

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.419
from both Republicans and Democrats

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.829
who are determined to get rid of it.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:11.939
They're worried the Chinese

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.769
government has too much influence on

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.539
the platform. Never mind that more

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.549
than 150 million Americans use

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.259
Tik Tok to express themselves

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.039
creatively, consume news they

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.649
wouldn't find elsewhere, and also to

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.149
keep themselves entertained.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.069
Nanny state politicians like Senator

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.079
Josh Hawley, President Joe Biden

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.579
think they should have the power to

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.139
control what kinds of foreign

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.389
content you are allowed to see.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.279
Not everyone in Washington thinks

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.529
banning Tik Tok is a good idea.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.569
Senator Rand Paul recently denounced

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.009
the idea of giving the Biden

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.199
administration more power to control

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.279
social media.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.719
I think we should beware of those

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.249
who peddle fear.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.139
I think we should beware of those

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.419
who use fear to coax Americans

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.399
to relinquish our liberties,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.079
to regulate and limit our First

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.309
Amendment rights.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.959
Paul is right.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.519
Here are three reasons why letting

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.779
the federal government prohibit

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.179
TikTok is an idiotic idea.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.098
First off, the dangers of Tik Tok

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:06.299
have been overstated.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.249
Yes, it's true you can find really

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.109
vile content on the platform.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.089
It's not all dance videos, recipes

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.319
and makeup tutorials.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.029
But that's not unique to Tik Tok.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.979
There's bad stuff in all corners

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.359
of the internet. Just because a

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.579
website or an app is bad sometimes

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.349
for some people doesn't mean we

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.759
should violate the First Amendment

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.559
rights of millions of others.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.449
Censorship is censorship.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.279
Even if it's well-intended, we

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.269
should leave the policing to

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.279
individuals, families and

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.079
schools to set restrictions on

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.609
social media usage.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.529
Not the federal government.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.939
Now, it's true that Tik Tok is

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.039
unique in that the Chinese Communist

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.809
Party can pressure the company in

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.099
ways that are bad.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.989
It's very likely that Tik Tok mutes

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.879
certain controversial subjects

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.409
and takes down the accounts of

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.119
dissidents in order to protect the

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.169
CCP.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.579
But the sad truth is the US

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.109
government has applied similar

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.149
pressure to American social media

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.579
companies like Facebook and Twitter.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.989
Journalists have discovered that

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.419
federal agencies, including the FBI,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.129
the Department of Homeland Security,

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.139
regularly asked Twitter to delete

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.698
content the government didn't

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:10.499
approve of. My own reporting, for

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.359
Reason, has revealed that the White

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.609
House and the CDC applied constant

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.499
pressure on Facebook

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.389
during the pandemic to restrict

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.069
speech. If members of Congress are

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.779
really so worried about government

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.219
propagandists controlling the

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.379
discourse on social media,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.459
well, they should start by putting

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.779
their own house in order.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.609
Lastly, any new law that

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.349
gives the feds the power to ban

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.179
TikTok could easily be

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.919
weaponized against other companies.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.299
The RESTRICT Act, which is

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.069
co-sponsored by Republican Senator

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.199
John Thune and Democratic Senator

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.389
Mark Warner, empowers the Commerce

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.919
Department to take action against

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.599
foreign threats on social media.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.819
But lawmakers, national intelligence

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.769
experts and mainstream media pundits

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.869
are constantly accusing Facebook

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.309
of allowing too much foreign

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.109
misinformation on the platform.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.539
This is the Patriot Act 2.0.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.099
If we give the government more tools

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.929
to police Tik Tok, they're going to

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.759
use them against all of us.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.739
So let's leave TikTok alone.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.939
Not just because of the dance

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.889
videos, but also because of

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:08.890
the First Amendment.

